  "title": "Mainstreaming climate change adaptation into urban planning: greyfield land redevelopment in Jena (Germany)",
  "summary": "In Jena, adaptation has been integrated in urban planning thanks to public awareness, public institutional support, and investments in collaboration and research. Detailed cost-benefit analyses inform decision-making for interventions such as the greyfield land redevelopment. Jena is a city of about 108,000 inhabitants and – due to its specific geographic location – is exposed to various climate change-related risks, whereas heatwaves are the most relevant. Climate projections for Jena expect a substantial increase of this risk in the future.",
